# Lasyd Prowler: "Renew -- {1}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put X +1/+1 counters on target creature, where X is the number of land cards in your graveyard. Activate only as a sorcery." Bot2 casts its own Prowler on turn 2 and mills a Forest (Bot2's graveyard, not counted). Bot1 casts one on turn 3 with two lands, milling two Forests, and Go for the Throat kills it on turn 5. With Memnite on the stack renew is refused (sorcery timing); then it is refused on Mox Jet (not a creature) and puts two counters (not three: the Prowler itself, Go for the Throat and Bot2's Forest are no X) on Bot2's Prowler, making it 7/7; Bot1's Prowler is exiled as the cost.

